{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 30,
    "dDurationMs": 5890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, you think Planet 9 exists with 99.8% probability?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5920,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Something like that. Yeah maybe 99.. I'll push it higher. 99.9% probability."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12400,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is wishful thinking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is. I mean if you're that sure, find it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19280,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the farthest reaches of our solar system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22080,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way past Neptune and Pluto,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24800,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a ninth planet may be lurking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27880,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's predicted to have a mass five times that of Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to orbit once every 10,000 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34400,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a highly elliptical, inclined orbit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why do some scientists suspect that such a strange object exists?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42680,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's what I've come to Caltech to find out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45280,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where do you like to do your work?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know I usually do it wherever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49600,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wherever I have a couple minutes of free time, I just do it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53040,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is where a lot of it is done."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55920,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My name is Konstantin Batygin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57800,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am a professor of planetary science at Caltech"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61240,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I do all kinds of astrophysics-y, planetary studies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including stuff about planet 9"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71240,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are variable transformations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73680,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll tell you where the planet 9 boundary lies it's like that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77120,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So everything to the left of that is all planet 9"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'm here to find out about hidden planets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83560,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how to find hidden planets with math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85840,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "okay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86480,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do we do that I mean do you want to start at the beginning of this sort of endeavor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91240,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or do you want to jump into planet 9? Where do you want to start?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93960,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, let's actually let's start at the beginning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96480,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the beginning, it has a long and beautiful history to it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101000,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And its origins dates back to 1781, I believe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105200,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When Uranus was first discovered by Herschel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109160,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when Herschel discovered Uranus he immediately realized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112600,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the star that was slowly moving across the sky,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116800,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had actually been imaged many many times before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119720,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was a matter of going back to old observations and kind of retracing the orbit that Uranus was following on on the sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127880,
    "dDurationMs": 8360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and astronomers and mathematicians at the time immediately noticed that there was a problem with orbit of this newly discovered planet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was deviating from where was supposed to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139360,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a French mathematician by the name of Urbain Le Verrier"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eventually did this beautiful and very complicated set of calculations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that said, \"Okay, if there is a planet is there, Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152040,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in that part of the sky, then we can explain the anomalous motion of Uranus.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when, once there was a mathematical prediction of where to look,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162960,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "astronomers were then able to discover Neptune with basically pinpoint accuracy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169480,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how quickly did they find neptune?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so this is a remarkable story. They found neptune in one night,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they knew exactly where to look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There could be a ninth planet. There's a lot of space for a ninth planet in the outer solar system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183480,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there's no good evidence for a ninth planet at the present time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186880,
    "dDurationMs": 7880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a particularly scary thing about the ninth planet is that a lot of people want to believe that there's a ninth planet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194760,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we all know there's this huge psychological bias"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198520,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To the effect that if you want to believe something is true, you will find evidence, real or not, that it's true"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205320,
    "dDurationMs": 7800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everyone and their brother in the last 170 years, have predicted planets beyond Neptune."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213120,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but all of these theories have failed to date"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216360,
    "dDurationMs": 9040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that we, meaning myself and my collaborator/partner-in-crime Mike Brown, are right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our understanding of the solar system has evolved dramatically in the last 20 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229640,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've discovered that there exists this one additional belt of icy debris called the Kuiper belt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236800,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these are kind of big icy asteroids that are maybe the size of LA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241360,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "floating around beyond Neptune"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245200,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Who's responsible for finding the Kuiper belt?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248040,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I found the Kuiper belt with my student Jane Luu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253240,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We were looking for anything actually beyond the orbit of Saturn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the puzzle, in 1985 the puzzle was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261080,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why is it that the inner part of the solar system is full of asteroids and comets and kind of things planets all this stuff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268760,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then when you go beyond Saturn, there's Uranus, there's Neptune, and there's Pluto and then that's it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276200,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why would the outer solar system be so empty?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278960,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a very simple question of the kind that I can understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282840,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the answer was well let's have a look!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285360,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know maybe it's not really empty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286920,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe it is in which case that would be interesting, but maybe it's not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290120,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we started a survey to find stuff beyond Saturn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294320,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we did the survey for a long time five years or something six years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298560,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and found actually nothing for that whole time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302760,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including nothing just beyond Saturn where we expected to find stuff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until finally in 1992 we got this thing way out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309400,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we could tell immediately it's way out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311680,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "45 or 50 au from the slow motion across the sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315920,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we found this thing out there, what we call now the first identified Kuiper belt object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321680,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's actually the second, because Pluto was misidentified back in 1930 for all sorts of reasons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "connected with sociology and propaganda and things like that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330920,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People wanted to find a planet, and so no matter what Pluto must be a planet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335600,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that process is continued. We have more than 2,000 of these objects now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339880,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so in 25 years 2,000 of these things have been found"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342720,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we think the population is vast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345160,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a billion things bigger than a kilometer across, maybe more. Maybe a couple billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350320,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's some of the more distant objects that appear to some people to show this orbital alignment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they have in particular very large perihelion distance so they never come close to the Sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362600,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they never come close to even Neptune"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at the most distant objects in this belt of debris called the Kuiper belt,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370240,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of their orbits kind of point into the same direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373560,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it possible that there are some going in the other direction and we just haven't found them?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377840,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379080,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah of course. That's a great question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381840,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Generically when you search for objects in the night sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386120,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are always what are called observational biases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you are always limited to finding objects only where you look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392760,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so this is a key question that you have to ask, right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396320,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it that we only found objects that are all pointing that way, right, their orbits pointing that way because we only look there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404160,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer is that there is a chance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406960,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That this is a this is all a false alarm, okay?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409680,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that chance is one in 500"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412320,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are bodies that occasionally will swing out into other directions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418840,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's more that overall if you look at it, there is an overall tendency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423040,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so here what we see is a pretty typical kind of simulation of the type that we do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we start the solar system in an initial kind of totally random state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436640,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where all the objects are pointing everywhere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439800,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for scale these pink circles here are Uranus and Neptune"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this long ellipse, this long pink ellipse is planet nine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these blue guys, these blue orbits are long period Kuiper belt objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455960,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ones that in the real solar system we see the clustering among"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460080,
    "dDurationMs": 11760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these gold or greenish ellipses are the more short period, more proximate members of the Kuiper belt which are not clustered at all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it takes a long time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but about two billion years into the evolution of the solar system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478240,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you begin to see the fact that objects that are collinear with planet nine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have all been scattered away, removed from the solar system dynamically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488720,
    "dDurationMs": 8200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the only kind of remaining members of the distant solar system the objects that point the opposite way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498960,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again it's a remarkable gravitational signature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502800,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gravitational one-way sign, if you will, that something is confining these orbits,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keeping them clustered, and pulling them all into the same plane"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512000,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, the experts, I think of Scott Shepard and Chad Raheel who first noticed this alignment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518680,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they call it a two point six sigma or result"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521760,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means that, you know, it doesn't really meet the threshold for acceptance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527480,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The scientific.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528200,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Would you be looking at five sigma? Is that.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530440,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean this the standard thing is three sigma, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533240,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but half of all 3 sigma results are wrong, is what I always say as an observer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538000,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the more significance the better, but two point six is not enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so even though these clusters of asteroid orbits in the Kuiper belt provide the best evidence for Planet 9,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547800,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a chance that further Kuiper belt observations will find different, uncluttered orbits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553280,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but regardless there are two other solar system mysteries that could be explained by the existence of Planet nine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560400,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These properties of Planet nine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562840,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they seem like kind of nuts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a period of ten thousand years, that's not like any of the planets that we have found"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569720,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why would we have such a strange planet hanging out out there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574240,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah great question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575320,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, none of this is reminiscent of anything solar system, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581120,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you for a second ignore the period right and ask yourself about the mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587400,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mass of five Earth masses. We don't have anything in the solar system that's five Earth masses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We go from one to 17, when we go from Earth to Neptune"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595560,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it wild?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596680,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually turns out this is the most common type of planet in the galaxy that we have discovered around other stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603240,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may be reversed:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604600,
    "dDurationMs": 9040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the fact that the solar system doesn't host a object which is five earth masses kind of closer to the Sun is actually kind of weird"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, five earth masses as it turns out, it's kind of standard outcome of plant formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618440,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are more wild things out there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620520,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oh and this is really my favorite aspect of the Planet nine hypothesis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626080,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's the fact that Planet 9 actively flips orbits on their side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632120,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you should not expect to find objects in the solar system that are flipped on their side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and are orbiting the Sun perpendicular to the planets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642000,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you should definitely not expect objects that are orbiting the solar system the wrong way, so to speak"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647640,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet we find them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right? They exist in the Kuiper belt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651040,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this has actually been a problem since before Planet 9 was even a thought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Planet nine has this intriguing mode of dynamical evolution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661920,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it instills upon distant orbits where it takes them and,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665320,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the expense of kind of circularizing these distant objects by making their orbits less elliptical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flips them upside down and then makes them more elliptical again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676440,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's a complicated dynamical evolution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678880,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and really at a detailed level you have to go to the computer simulations to understand how it works"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685320,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the key kind of product of the existence of Planet 9"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691120,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the expectation that such objects would exist, and we see them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694520,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I think, really there isn't another kind of natural mechanism to generate these highly inclined bodies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702440,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know you have the plane of most of the the bodies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then some of the bodies are there apparently have their orbits almost tilted up to 90 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711080,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that just weird, or is that stronger evidence for.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716640,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's one of the things that they claim to explain with the planet 9 hypothesis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's a good thing in favor of the hypothesis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724240,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but again, you know you need to find the planet to be sure what's going on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728160,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the region that we have not yet been able to probe, because we can't see faint enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734600,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know. Yeah. We don't know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when do you think we're gonna find Planet 9?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741040,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a great question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743360,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So observing the sky has proven to be an extreme challenge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749760,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the search for planet 9 is extremely difficult"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753520,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just kind of dim enough at the outer parts of its orbit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it can be discovered with current telescopes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761840,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you, but everything has to go right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763800,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by everything has to go right I mean no moon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the atmosphere has to be calm so that the light is not messed up by the turbulence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771120,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such nights do come around every year, but they don't come around very often"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776800,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so since 2017 we've had exactly two successful runs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783760,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right, successful observational runs where we had sort of a string of nights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787960,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where we could take pictures of the same part of the sky over and over again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793120,
    "dDurationMs": 9680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we are about 20%, maybe a little bit more now 25% done with the survey that we are carrying out to search for planet 9"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802800,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if things go at this rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it might take about a decade"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807800,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think the commencement of the LSST telescope,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is coming online 2022,23"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814800,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's gonna help a lot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816200,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because that's going to first of all discover many more of these objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we'll be able to refine the theoretical model better"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825560,
    "dDurationMs": 9800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also just by direct observation it'll either find planet 9, or rule out a big chunk of its orbit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we could kind of zero in that way a lot more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's a, it's an iterative process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would guesstimate a decade or less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846840,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So volumetrically we've discovered most of the solar system in the last 25 years, something like that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852720,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you mean volumetrically?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854120,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean that the volume of the region occupied by the planets is very small, it's 10,000 cubic astronomical units"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862280,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as you go further out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know the volume of that sphere that encapsulates all the objects that we've been able to observe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868480,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is just going up dramatically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you go ten times further out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872640,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we are now just about able to do,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875640,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you increase the volume that you're looking at by a factor of a thousand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878520,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a whole bunch of stuff going on, you know solar system is, to me, an unknown place"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, we fool ourselves to thinking that we know everything about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just because we've only been looking close and we have a lot of data from spacecrafts and so on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the further away you go, the less known it is, and the more mysterious it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898080,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this ninth planet thing is part of that, because essentially when you go far enough away from the Sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903320,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's enough room to hide almost anything you want"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will be so faint you can put almost anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910840,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Big planets, small planets, whatever you want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913800,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We would not have seen it yet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915760,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If or when you do find it, who gets to name it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh that's something we don't think about and don't talk about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925480,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You don't have a name in the back of your head?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928080,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The... Only David Bowie."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930640,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah there's a online petition on change.org to name Planet nine David Bowie,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I thought it was kind of silly initially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938600,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then there's this whole David Bowie like mythology that you could create"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if it has moons you could have Ziggy Stardust, Starman, and all of these things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947640,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, you know I was kinda like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951360,
    "dDurationMs": 7720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not saying that seriously but also it would be kind of remarkable if we had Jupiter Saturn Uranus Neptune and David Bowie"
    } ]
  } ]
}
